WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.259
Quite a few of you guys have been asking us
to make a video on the real differences between

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:07.379
the iPhone 11 and the 11 Pro, so here it is!

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:10.500
As well as the question of which one of these
premium iPhones you should buy.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.510
The answer actually boils down to something
very simple.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.290
I’ll explain in just a bit.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.779
If you’re a fan of colors, you get a lot
more options on the iPhone 11, while the 11

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:25.039
Pro is a bit more limited, but the new midnight
green color is much nicer than I expected.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:28.939
On the back, they get a new unique square
bump that’s machined out of a single sheet

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:34.010
of glass, with the 11 getting two circular
camera bumps, while the 11 Pro gets a nicely

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.790
arranged 3 bumps that in my opinion, screams
premium.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.520
More on those cameras in just a minute.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.470
The Matte glass back looks really nice on
the 11 Pro, while the 11 gets a glossy back

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.040
with matte on the square bump.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.670
I personally love the smooth finish of the
11 Pro’s matte glass, which is also very

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:55.440
fingerprint and microscratch resistant, but
others may not like how slippery it is and

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.610
they may prefer the iPhone 11 for the extra
grip in the hand.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:04.239
The 11 Pro also has a glossy stainless steel
frame which feels very grippy and premium,

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:08.570
but it’s more susceptible to microscratches,
while the regular 11 has an aluminum frame

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.920
that Apple’s been using since the iPhone
6, but if you like to use a case with your

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.259
iPhone, the difference in feel won’t matter.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:20.939
With last year’s iPhones, the XR was noticeably
thicker than the XS, but this year, the 11

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:24.350
Pro got a bit thicker, so you won’t really
notice a big difference in your hand like

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.409
you did last year.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:31.810
The 11 Pro comes in two sizes, 5.8 inches,
which I personally feel is too small, and

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:37.189
6.5 inches, which is nice for the large display,
but a bit uncomfortable to hold in one hand.

00:01:37.189 --> 00:01:43.200
So in my opinion, the 6.1” size of the Phone
11 is actually the perfect middle-ground,

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.539
offering a large display while feeling perfect
in the hand.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:51.909
The iPhone 11 features the exact same LCD
display from last year’s XR, with less than

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:56.509
1080p resolution, which is a bummer, but you
can’t really tell with regular use unless

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:59.590
you pixel peep or watch a very high quality
video.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.659
It’s got the same True Tone technology and
excellent color accuracy with P3 wide-color

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:05.659
gamut.

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.360
The iPhone 11 Pro’s display has a much higher
resolution, a much better contrast ratio thanks

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.299
to it being an OLED display, and it got even
brighter this year.

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:19.360
The main difference is that you can’t watch
high-quality HDR content on the regular 11,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.849
and you’ll have more trouble seeing the
display when you’re outside in broad daylight.

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:27.040
The benefit of the iPhone 11 Pro’s OLED
display is that using dark mode or a darker

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.040
wallpaper will actually save battery life
because the individual pixels emit their own

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.189
light and can actually turn off completely
when displaying black.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:40.519
One of the biggest downsides with last year’s
iPhone XR was that it didn’t get 3D Touch

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:45.060
like on the XS, but this year, even the 11
Pro doesn’t get it anymore.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.939
Now the one display difference that matters
the most to me is that the display bezels

00:02:48.939 --> 00:02:54.269
on the 11 are noticeably larger than the ones
on the 11 Pro, which already seem large compared

00:02:54.269 --> 00:02:56.500
to other phones like the Note 10 Plus.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.069
So with all of the visible differences out
of the way, let’s get into feature differences.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:05.330
Something new this year is that the iPhone
11 Pro actually comes with an 18W fast-charger

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:10.360
in the box instead of the super old and slow
5w charger with the 11.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.459
Now if the slow 5w charger is keeping you
from buying the iPhone 11, it shouldn’t.

00:03:14.459 --> 00:03:19.709
The 11 actually supports the same exact fast-charging
speed as the 11 Pro, you just have to buy

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:24.780
the fast-charger separately, which unfortunately,
is about $30 from Apple.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.129
Thankfully, you can buy a charger with the
same exact 18 watts of fast-charging speed

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:31.700
for only $16 right now on Amazon.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.469
We’ll drop a link down below.

00:03:33.469 --> 00:03:39.540
Now if I could explain the iPhone 11 Pro and
Pro Max in just two words, they would be battery

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.540
life.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.400
My 11 Pro Max is the first phone I’ve ever
had where I can do anything on my phone and

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.719
no longer have to even think about battery
life.

00:03:47.719 --> 00:03:50.900
It’s so great that I’ve actually stopped
checking it throughout the day.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.900
Now the battery life on the 11 isn’t as
good, but it’s still rated for an extra

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.870
hour over the XR, which already had better
battery life than last year’s iPhone XS

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.800
Max, so it’s still pretty great.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:08.230
The iPhone 11 Pro also gets better water resistance,
lasting 30 minutes in up to 13 feet of water,

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:12.379
which is more than the deepest point of a
regular swimming pool, while the 11 lasts

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:15.530
the same 30 minutes in up to 6 and a half
feet of water.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:19.530
Other than all of that, and a couple of small
differences in the cameras, which I’ll mention

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.690
in a moment, everything else is basically
the same.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:28.091
You get the same A13 Bionic chip, which is
the fastest processor on any smartphone, and

00:04:28.091 --> 00:04:33.840
you even get the same 4GB of RAM, whereas
last year’s XR only got 3GB.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.669
You get the same Face ID system, the same
U1 chip, the same spatial audio speakers with

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:46.310
Dolby Atmos support, the same WiFi 6 and Gigabit
LTE speed, the same Dual-Sim support, and

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.330
the same wireless charging speed.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:52.419
And now for the cameras, you get the same
exact wide and ultrawide lenses.

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:57.389
The photos and videos coming out of these
two are literally identical, with the same

00:04:57.389 --> 00:05:04.680
video recording features, the same crazy good
stabilization, night mode, 2nd gen smart HDR,

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.970
and basically every other feature available
on the 11 Pro.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.639
However, the one thing the Pro has is the
telephoto lens.

00:05:11.639 --> 00:05:13.810
And it’s good for a couple of things.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:18.620
First is being able to zoom in more for photos
and videos, and second, you can take more

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.900
realistic close-up portrait photos.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:25.610
If you try a close-up portrait on the iPhone
11’s wide lens, it greatly distorts the

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:30.500
shape of the face, so you have to take a step
back, snap the photo and then crop into it

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.229
in post to get a close-up, which can reduce
quality.

00:05:33.229 --> 00:05:36.240
And that’s basically the only difference
in the cameras.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.199
So if you’re still trying to figure out
if you should buy the iPhone 11 or the 11

00:05:40.199 --> 00:05:42.680
Pro, I’ll make it really simple for you.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:46.821
If you’re coming from a premium smartphone
that packs a high-quality OLED display, like

00:05:46.821 --> 00:05:52.330
the iPhone X, you should go for the 11 Pro
or 11 Pro Max, because you’ll probably notice

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:57.690
the lack of contrast on the 11’s display,
as well as the thicker bezels.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:02.000
But if you’re coming from an older LCD-packing
phone with large top and bottom bezels like

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:08.770
the iPhone 6, 7, or 8, then you should go
with the iPhone 11 and spend the extra $300-400

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.650
difference on something else, like a $16 fast-charger
by using the link in the description.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:18.319
If you enjoyed this comparison, make sure
to Tap Like &amp; click the circle above to subscribe.

00:06:18.319 --> 00:06:26.880
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video!

